      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "George Washington’s 1753–54 expeditions highlighted Fairbank’s strategic spot, sparking frontier outposts after the French and Indian War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fairbank_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fairbank grew as part of Fayette County’s coal mining boom, though specific mines in the town are scarcely recorded.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fairbank_pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fairbank’s post office began serving residents in 1906, marking its first formal federal presence.",
